    "movement": "A low broad antlion advances on alternating tripods with full equal individual foot travel, firm pointed-talon contacts and nearly steady front shell. The faster scuttle has larger sweeps and quicker cadence. Four real overlapping posterior rows hang centered behind the anterior shell.",
